  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Remove the synthetic `contact_{guid}` SPE container-permission POST in `GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs` (~lines 242-257). Under the broker-only model (ADR-028 A1) it is vestigial — external users never reach SPE directly; all access is app-only. Keep the `sprk_externalrecordaccess` create and the participation cache invalidation intact.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    You are a BFF engineer removing a now-vestigial SPE container membership write from the grant path while preserving the three-plane access record + cache invalidation.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The synthetic `contact_{guid}` SPE container-permission POST in `GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs` (~lines 242-257) is removed; the endpoint still creates the `sprk_externalrecordaccess` record and invalidates the participation cache.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Under broker-only (ADR-028 Amendment A1), external users never authenticate to SPE directly — all external SPE access is app-only via the BFF. The historical `contact_{guid}` synthetic container-permission write (a hangover from the B2B-guest model) grants nothing meaningful now and is an anti-pattern to keep. This task removes it while leaving the authoritative `sprk_externalrecordaccess` create + ADR-009 cache invalidation untouched.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: the grant path. Broker-only (Amendment A1) makes the synthetic SPE container grant vestigial — remove it; external SPE access remains app-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-FR-10">Scope: the retained behavior. The `/grant` endpoint MUST still create `sprk_externalrecordaccess` and invalidate the participation cache — only the synthetic `contact_{guid}` SPE permission POST is removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-009">Scope: cache invalidation. Participation-cache invalidation on grant MUST remain (unchanged).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this BFF task. State the §10 BFF Hygiene Placement Justification in the PR description (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`), and report BFF compressed publish size + diff vs baseline (~49.63 MB) confirming the ≤60 MB ceiling (NFR-01).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read `GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs` and locate the synthetic `contact_{guid}` SPE container-permission POST (~lines 242-257).</step>
    <step>Remove that POST and any now-dead local variables/imports solely supporting it; keep the `sprk_externalrecordaccess` create and the cache-invalidation call.</step>
    <step>Confirm the endpoint still compiles and the grant + invalidation flow is intact.</step>
    <step>Build and run `dotnet publish -c Release`; record compressed size + diff vs the ~49.63 MB baseline.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output>`GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs` with the synthetic SPE container grant removed.</output>
    <output>Retained `sprk_externalrecordaccess` create + participation-cache invalidation.</output>
    <output>BFF publish-size report (compressed size + diff).</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`/grant` still creates the `sprk_externalrecordaccess` access record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`/grant` still invalidates the participation cache.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no synthetic `contact_{guid}` SPE container permission is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing grant tests pass (or are updated) with the synthetic write removed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF compressed publish size is reported with diff and stays ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Modify-only — no §11 component justification required; the §10 BFF Hygiene note (Placement Justification + publish-size report) still applies. Startable (no deps). Grant-without-synthetic-SPE is also covered by the task-030 tests.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
